  "resourceBoundary": {
    "maxRequestBytes": 65536,
    "requestBytesByOperation": {
      "command.document.object.vector.edit": 65536,
      "command.document.object.parametric.edit": 4096,
      "command.document.object.path.effects.edit": 4096
    },
    "maxReadResponseBytes": 4096,
    "policy": "Complete original UTF-8 request envelope: vector edit is bounded at 65536 bytes; parametric and path-effect edits remain 4096 bytes. Replies remain 4096 bytes. Larger requests are refused, never split or truncated. Complete correlated retained receipt or typed refusal."
  },
  "semantics": "Create, replace and delete one editable open or closed vector path (nullable fill and stroke with alpha, hasRealStroke, width, cap, join, miter limit, dash, paint order, opacity, optional pressure ribbon fields, paramShape and boxAngle); translate, scale or re-parameterize a dynamic rect, ellipse or star; replace the complete ordered path-effect stack of a layer (zigzag, roughen; storage order is evaluation order, an empty stack is authored). One request is one atomic revision and one undo entry; an effective no-op keeps presence, bytes, history and redo and reports applied=false. The owner allocates the id of a created stroke (the record names an empty strokeId) and reports it. A locked Drawing layer, a layer with an active path effect, a reference scope and a pressure ribbon (for parameter edits) are typed refusals. Source geometry is never mutated by an effect: the stack is evaluated at a pinned snapshot and frame. No JS or Paper writer, no optimistic mutation. Stored vectorExt.fillGradient admits exactly two-stop linear/radial baseline paint, with document-world endpoints and original hex color strings/stop order. The existing baseline stroke producer maps fillGradient without a second owner. Other stop counts and pressure-gradient combinations remain unavailable; no installed gradient/UI acceptance is implied. The batch step restyle (#2372) changes only the style members it names (hex fill and stroke with alpha, a positive width, an opacity in 0..1) on a presented record or stored item: fill and stroke reach only paint the record already has, a ribbon is inked by its fill and rescales its width profile before the engine rebuilds its outline and linked fill, opacity is the fill alpha or else the item opacity, a text block takes the fill as its colour and the opacity as its alpha, an image takes the opacity; bitmap brushes, brush dabs and a texture anchor whose copies are stored are typed refusals. The hit-test listing carries the style a panel shows. SEL-STYLE2 adds the members fillEnabled and strokeEnabled (turning one on names its colour in fill or stroke; a ribbon skips the fill switch and its stroke switch is its ink alpha), cap, join, miter (1..1000), dashOffset, paintOrder and strokeStyle (solid, dashed or dotted, the dash pattern scaled by the stroke width), reaching plain records (a ribbon takes only the paint order), brushPreset (a built-in or project preset key, or none: strips the texture and restamps a plain stroke as a seeded anchor, leaving a ribbon, a Fill Brush shape or an unstroked record as it is; stored dabs are a typed refusal) maskFeather (the shared feather of every mask in the named mask's cell), maskMode (add, subtract or intersect: the named mask's own mode) and unmask (true: the named mask becomes a normal shape again, its mask tags dropped and its geometry and paint kept) and fillGradient (#2372: a stored two-stop linear or radial gradient in record space with #rrggbb[aa] stop colours, which also makes the flat fill its first stop when the record had no gradient, or null to return to the flat fill; a pressure ribbon, a mask, a bitmap brush and a stamped dab are a typed refusal); each of these five stands alone. A batch reshape with a matrix moves, scales or turns a mask like any other vector record. One restyle batch is one revision and one undo entry. A batch may span scene-root layers (#2372: a Select over several layers restyles or transforms in one revision and one undo entry); every step is guarded by its own layer's lock and path effects, one refused step refuses the batch with nothing written, and only a trimEnds batch is one layer. A create, replace, delete or batch may name a declared component as the context of its targets (#2256, the entered component of the baseline enterSymbol): the edit lands in that component's own layers and records as one revision and one undo entry, every instance re-renders, the scene root is untouched, a context the document does not declare is an invalid_request, and the copy key, Fill Brush and the other families stay scene-only.",
  "commonErrorCodes": [
    "invalid_request",
    "wrong_instance",
    "wrong_document",
    "stale_revision",
    "unavailable",
    "not_found",
    "cancelled_before_dispatch",
    "internal"
  ],
